.TH telinit 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
telinit \- change the run level
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B telinit
.IR runlevel | \fBq\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B telinit
tells
.B init
to change run level.  It writes the request to
.B /var/run/initctl
and signals process 1.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B 0
to
.B 6
The numbered run levels.  Which of them do what is set in
.BR /etc/inittab .
.TP
.BR s ", " S
Single user.
.TP
.B q
Re-read
.B /etc/inittab
without changing level.  Use this after editing it.
.SH NOTES
One character only.
.B telinit 12
is an invalid run level, not run level 12.
.PP
.BR shutdown (1)
and
.BR reboot (1)
are the ordinary way to stop the machine;
.B telinit
is for changing what is running while it stays up.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shutdown (1),
.BR reboot (1),
.BR kill (1)
